WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:15.113
City, or the Vatican, as it is commonly known, lies within the city of Rome.

2
00:00:16.174 --> 00:00:19.176
Despite its name, Vatican City is actually a country!

3
00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:24.161
This country is home to the leadership of the Catholic Church and has a rich history.

4
00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:27.864
St. Peter's Basilica is its most famous site.

5
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.061
The church was named for St.

6
00:00:30.121 --> 00:00:33.302
Peter, who was Jesus' favorite and most faithful follower.

7
00:00:34.302 --> 00:00:36.643
St. Peter was an early Christian leader in Rome.

8
00:00:37.624 --> 00:00:40.065
At that time, the Romans persecuted Christians.

9
00:00:41.005 --> 00:00:44.206
In the year 64, he was executed by Roman officials.

10
00:00:45.307 --> 00:00:48.368
He was buried in a graveyard on a hill called the Vatican.

11
00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:53.390
As the number of Christians grew, a large church was built on the site where St.

12
00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.290
Peter was buried.

13
00:00:55.151 --> 00:00:55.731
Soon St.

14
00:00:55.771 --> 00:00:59.793
Peter's Basilica became the main church of the pope, the leader of the Catholic Church.

15
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:02.854
By 1506 St.

16
00:01:02.894 --> 00:01:04.695
Peter's Basilica was falling apart.

17
00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:08.576
It was also too small for all the church officials who worked there.

18
00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:14.999
So Pope Julius II demolished it and built a huge new church with a 42-meter-tall dome.

19
00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:18.720
This new church was not fully completed until 1626.

20
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.041
The new St.

21
00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:24.443
Peter's Basilica became the largest church in the world at the time.

22
00:01:25.523 --> 00:01:27.084
And because of its connection to St.

23
00:01:27.124 --> 00:01:31.009
Peter, it also became one of Christianity's most important churches.

24
00:01:31.889 --> 00:01:33.510
The church is still in use today.

25
00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.931
Another famous religious building in the Vatican is the Sistine Chapel.

26
00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:42.312
The chapel was built between 1477 and 1481.

27
00:01:43.832 --> 00:01:49.254
The rectangular building looks plain and simple on the outside, but there is a treasure of Renaissance art

28
00:01:49.374 --> 00:01:56.776
inside. Pope Julius II needed an artist to decorate the chapel's ceiling—all eight hundred square meters of it.

29
00:01:57.824 --> 00:02:01.146
He hired Michelangelo for the job, which was a surprising choice.

30
00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:05.088
Michelangelo was known for his sculpture, not his painting.

31
00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:10.912
For four years Michelangelo painted the ceiling with his head tilted up and his hands extended above his

32
00:02:10.972 --> 00:02:13.993
body. His labor was an amazing feat.

33
00:02:14.814 --> 00:02:17.395
The result was an even more amazing work of art.

34
00:02:18.496 --> 00:02:21.618
The ceiling's nine main sections illustrate scenes from the Bible.

35
00:02:22.398 --> 00:02:25.540
Paintings of people and angels from the Bible decorate the borders.

36
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.523
Thousands of tourists visit the Sistine Chapel each day to see Michelangelo's magnificent art.

37
00:02:33.864 --> 00:02:34.264
Like St.

38
00:02:34.304 --> 00:02:37.386
Peter's Basilica, the Sistine Chapel is still used today.

39
00:02:38.187 --> 00:02:43.330
In fact, the chapel is used for one of the Catholic Church's most important ceremonies—the election of a

40
00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:43.890
new pope.

41
00:02:44.871 --> 00:02:50.334
When a pope dies or resigns, church officials called cardinals come to the Vatican to choose their new

42
00:02:50.394 --> 00:02:53.776
leader. The cardinals stay locked inside the Vatican.

43
00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.003
They have no contact with the outside world until they elect a new pope.

44
00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:02.647
Every day during this time, the cardinals go into the Sistine Chapel.

45
00:03:03.547 --> 00:03:06.030
They pray about which cardinal should be the next pope.

46
00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.093
Then elections are held each day until a new pope is chosen.

47
00:03:11.054 --> 00:03:13.556
The cardinals vote by writing a name on a piece of paper.

48
00:03:14.396 --> 00:03:18.019
The votes are counted, and then all the ballots are burned in the chapel's furnace.

49
00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:24.468
Outside the chapel, crowds gather, eagerly watching for signs of smoke from the chapel's chimney.

50
00:03:24.488 --> 00:03:27.750
Black smoke tells the crowd that the cardinals have not yet chosen a new pope.

51
00:03:28.731 --> 00:03:32.213
White smoke and the ringing of bells mean that a new pope has been elected.

52
00:03:33.174 --> 00:03:34.955
How is the black or white smoke made?

53
00:03:35.976 --> 00:03:39.318
In the past, wet straw was added to the fire to turn the smoke black.

54
00:03:40.199 --> 00:03:42.921
But sometimes the smoke looked gray instead of black or white.

55
00:03:44.562 --> 00:03:47.824
So nowadays chemicals are used to produce the black or white smoke.

56
00:03:49.185 --> 00:03:53.528
After the election the new pope changes from his red cardinal's clothing into the white robes of the

57
00:03:53.568 --> 00:03:56.285
pope. Then he comes out and greets the people.

58
00:03:57.285 --> 00:04:01.267
He is now the leader of the Catholic Church—and a country, Vatican City.

59
00:04:02.447 --> 00:04:04.348
Vatican City isn't just any country.

60
00:04:05.108 --> 00:04:09.790
It has a population of around only one thousand and covers less than half a square kilometer.

61
00:04:10.651 --> 00:04:12.751
This makes it the smallest country in the world.

62
00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:19.074
Vatican City is definitely small, but its history, art, and religious significance are huge.

63
00:04:20.294 --> 00:04:22.475
No wonder millions of people visit each year!
